WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:10.060 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the ex-house stands in the hills around  kabrel northeast of barcelona it's  unusual shape is best appreciated from  above a concrete building appears to be  floating it's exactly what owner de  Bourg LIGO had dreamed of hello welcome  to Barcelona welcome to my home come in  and I'll show you the house the  two-story building has 350 square meters  of living space the main living area is  on the lower floor this is our living  room where we spend lots of time with  our friends meeting up and having fun  and most of all enjoying the views which  are really awesome six meter high glass  facades allow fantastic views from every  room on Keir days you can even see the  Mediterranean  the owner chose the X shape to enable  views of both the mountains and the  scene the back of the house offers  privacy from neighbors while the front  offers panoramic views nature played an  important role in the construction of  the house we wanted to integrate it into  the project we couldn't change the  landscape because it was already there  so we had to construct the house in a  way that enabled it to fit into the  natural environment in contacto continua  meant a palace well de Berkeley Co was  planning the house with the architects  he came up with a fitting concept for  the furniture simple and modern  Glee goes favorite spot is right next to  his office on the upper floor this is  where he comes to relax clear lines and  colors dominate the interior design  combined with classics like these  Charles Eames armchairs what I love  about classic furniture is the history  behind it it's the story behind the  furniture that I like the architecture  the engineering and the people who  created it I didn't want extravagant  furniture I wanted something classic  something recognizable adjoining the  living room is a kitchen with an open  dining area the 7 meter long marble  table was designed specially for the  house it's integrated cooking surface  was tailor-made in Germany  the building's axes divided into  different kinds of living space the  house was designed by architect Eduardo  Carrabelle the concept was a challenge  as it was one of the first houses ever  built in the shape the construction  process of this house was also an  exercise in almost an experimentation we  were called by the client because we had  some experience doing concrete houses  and he wanted to test the construction  technique of shotcrete of projected  concrete that is normally used for  bridges and tunnels to build residential  spaces so the walls were projected with  concrete and then we were pouring six  metre tall walls with just one frame in  one side and the other one was was  projected the experiment was successful  not expensive the highest cost 2 million  euros to build it's mainly made of  concrete and glass in the master bedroom  the windows reach from the ceiling to  the floor when I wake up and open my  eyes the first thing I see from my bed  is the nature the position of the  bedroom is really nice and it was  conceived that way you don't see the  house or anything else you only see  nature as if you were sleeping outside  de Bourg legal and his family have lived  in the ex house for a year now enjoying  365 days of breathtaking views  [Music]

